// Title: Custom File Open Handler Executes PowerShell
// Sigma ID: 7530b96f-ad8e-431d-a04d-ac85cc461fdc
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: CD_R0M_
// Date: 2022-06-11 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1202
// Description: Detects the abuse of custom file open handler, executing powershell
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://news.sophos.com/en-us/2022/02/01/solarmarker-campaign-used-novel-registry-changes-to-establish-persistence/?cmp=30728
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_custom_file_open_handler_powershell_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "shell\\open\\command*" and (RegistryValueData contains "powershell" and RegistryValueData contains "-command")
